  "issue": {
    "body": "We should probably hide away `Path` and `Include` as implementation details for now, and instead focus on making the app and router interfaces match up.\r\n\r\nEg:\r\n\r\n```python\r\napp = Router()\r\n\r\n@app.route('/')\r\nasync def homepage(...):\r\n    ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nor...\r\n\r\n```python\r\napp = Router()\r\n\r\napp.mount('/admin', AdminApp)\r\napp.mount('/articles', BlogArticles)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis'll mean that a `Router` instance strictly gives you a subset of the functionality that a `Starlette` instance offers.\r\n\r\nRefs #122 ",
    "body_last_edited_at": "2018-10-18T07:36:34Z",
    "closed_at": "2018-10-26T09:30:55Z",
    "created_at": "2018-10-18T07:33:36Z",
